    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nAs a new mini.jump2d user, I got very surprised by the fact that, when using `MiniJump2d.builtin_opts.single_character`, there is a delay in the feedback message that prompts the user to type a character. When using EasyMotion, that prompt is immediate (so you know that you've triggered, which sometimes one does by mistake). When I was using the defaults of mini.jump2d, I also get immediate feedback that the mapping is pressed and the plugin is waiting for my input.\n\nI think the timeout to the `defer_fn` in `H.getcharstr` is a bit unintuitive/unexpected. I certainly would love to be able to customize it to 0 myself. Besides the customization, I think reconsidering the default is perhaps also a good idea.\n\nThank you very much for mini! :-)",
