            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> As a new mini.jump2d user, I got very surprised by the fact that, when using `MiniJump2d.builtin_opts.single_character`, there is a delay in the feedback message that prompts the user to type a character. When using EasyMotion, that prompt is immediate (so you know that you've triggered, which sometimes one does by mistake). When I was using the defaults of mini.jump2d, I also get immediate feedback that the mapping is pressed and the plugin is waiting for my input.\n\nThat is only a helper (purely informational) message. Pressing a character can be done immediately. This behavior is the same across all modules that have this type of \"wait for the user input but it is not a regular mapping\" behavior. It can be disabled with [`config.silent = true`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2431902e78b76f435542d1e606f08475360068ca/doc/mini-jump2d.txt#L212-L213) which is the same across all modules.\n\nSo I'd close this as not planned.\n\n---\n\nThe initial idea was to be helpful first time users who might not necessarily be aware of the workflow. Showing the message immediately is too noisy for other users who are expected to press a key within one second.\n\nBut as this is not the first misunderstanding of how it works, something has to be done here. I have couple of ideas, but they require some time to become more mature. ",
